{"kind":"report","text":"Independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of request/receipt-checkpoint-freshness at exact clean pushed head 4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd (cut from main 72c3b724dbf5919a59a8ae7aefe6c9ba3d209605), against codex ratified ruling #11588, which I read from the durable log myself before examining the code. VERDICT: approved.\n\nARCHITECTURE. The change is confined to layer 5, the Workroom application interpreter: gate and temporal rule live in internal/workroom/fold.go (receiptCheckpointSettles/causesSettledAtReceipt, called once per basis edge from the staleness loop); kernel and cmd/ are untouched, and docs/reference/architecture.md documents the contract change in this same head with its candidate artifact published here. Contracts elsewhere preserved: describes_superseded_world handling is unchanged in every branch (checked across all early returns, plus end-to-end case 7).\n\nSECURITY. The checkpoint fails closed on every axis examined: effective valid prospective receipt AND plan carrying BOTH merge_changed_paths (canonical: strictly increasing plus JSON round-trip equality) and merge_left_live; direct citation of that receipt; author match; exact merge_head and declared successor path. Malformed half-pair, legacy receipt without the pair, and unrelated borrowers gain nothing. Undated causes refuse settlement (when == 0), so a cause the fold cannot place in time can never read as settled. Left-live verification is read nowhere in the gate, so unverified testimony confers no freshness authority. No new untrusted-input surface beyond existing event parsing; no secrets involved. No unresolved security defect.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Nothing rises to changes-requested. Two latent notes for maintainers, neither load-bearing today: causesSettledAtReceipt reuses visited as cycle-guard-and-memo returning true on revisit (safe while any unsettled cause aborts the whole walk; unlike stalenessCoveredByMergePlan it does not backtrack), and unknown-event handling differs between the two walkers (consistent with semantics: a never-materialized id carries no cause). The eleven-versus-twelve count reconciliation holds: fourteen test rows reach twelve distinct decision points in fold.go, with shared rows explicitly disclaimed in comments rather than counted as guards.\n\nMANDATORY EXAMINATIONS. (1) Rule match confirmed clause by clause: the receipt itself can never qualify as a settled dependent (asserts render as notes, not artifacts; plan keys name artifacts only), so it stays historically stale; post-receipt dated causes propagate; the walk roots at the receipt so its own retirement still flares the successor; left-live verification appears nowhere in the gate. (2) Undated fail-closed confirmed with a constructed ghost-retirement case; a mutation dropping the undated refusal fails exactly that test. (3) Confinement confirmed: one call site, per-basis, bool-only gate receiving no world map. (4) Guard mapping verified by mutation testing in a throwaway source copy, pristine restored after each cut: each named guard flips its case red on single removal; both disclaimed claims hold verbatim - the legacy-receipt neither-field row pins nothing distinct (each presence clause catches it under the other's removal), and left-live orthogonality is correctly shaped as add-to-break because no removal can make the gate read testimony it never reads. No fixture asserts mechanism-fired over right-outcome: assertions sit on projected row outcomes with inert-fixture sentinels throughout. (5) Both white-box tests justified: the undated state is transactionally unreachable through Fold (reaching it would resurrect succeeded retirements on withdrawal), and forcing accounting flags over a nil plan is the only way to hold the plan guard down distinctly against a future parse reorder. (6) Empirical reproduction CONFIRMED independently: binaries built from git archives at main 72c3b724dbf5919a59a8ae7aefe6c9ba3d209605 and this head, same query against the same log via verified-local fallback, identical frontier depth 11754: successors 13c9a0a2861529a51aacfc20bf721135f951fe25 and 1fb4d37a6a54a73df67311e9f2967bfecba535d1 of receipt 03c440d4 report stale under the old binary and current under the new. One factual correction for the record, not a defect: those successors stand at paths cmd/gs and docs, not among the five paths enumerated in the request text. (7) The workroom-fold@11 to @12 bump forces full snapshot replay through the composite profile key; a mutation reverting only the bump fails the rebuilt-cache test, so that test genuinely discriminates.\n\nCHECKS RUN at the exact tree: gofmt clean on changed files; go build ./... green; go vet ./... green; go test -count=1 ./internal/workroom/... ./internal/app/... green; git diff --check clean. The full ./... suite re-run was not executed inside this review pass; the two affected packages were exercised exhaustively instead.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c0c5bcedaf44887727b22615d378fdaf6787d5f","head":"4981c6d0f571c9a7504311f83c6cb08517be0acd","verdict":"approved"}}